<<bg town_night>>

By the time Ariel came back to the church, the sky went dark.
The people in town were settling down, and the air was getting chilly.

<<bg kosciol_night>>

The priest walked inside the building and sighed loudly.
Well, that was… a day.
It was A DAY for sure.
Now he just wanted to take his bags, walk to the presbytery, and go to sleep.
He heard some rustling echoing through the empty church. 

<<show ariel basic left>>

Ariel: Father Faust..? 

Silence. Maybe he’s hearing things?
It’s possible, he’s actually pretty damn tired. 

???: Hihihi.

//(muzyka typu scawwy exorcism)

//(Ariel blush)

Ariel jumped.
Oh no, no, he definitely heard that.
Someone's here.
Laughing.
And it definitely wasn’t Faust. 

???: Oh, you’re cute.
???: Cute and stupid.
???: Mhm!
???: Perfect!
???: That’s how I like them, you know?
???: Cute, dumb, naive, and sooo, sooo pure.
???: It’s going to be so fun corrupting your soul-!

Ariel: Wha-..?

???: Hihihi.

//(Ariel basic)

Another giggle.
And from the mist before Ariel's eyes, a silhouette grew more and more vivid.

<<show ludus basic right>>

It wasn’t Faust.
Nor Marchein, nor Lilian.
It was someone completely different.
Something completely different.
A demon.
A real… real demon.
Ariel wanted to run away, but all of a sudden his legs felt too heavy to move.
His breathing grew ragged. 

The Demon: Oh, you’re scared!
The Demon: Why? What do you think I'll do?
The Demon: Kill you? Eat your soul? Drink your blood?
The Demon: Oh please, that would be extremely boring.
The Demon: No, no, I’m here to have fun!

Ariel: W-What do you mean fun?
Ariel: Who are you?
Ariel: W-why are you here?

//(Ludus silly)

The Demon: Woah, hold your horses!
The Demon: That’s a shit ton of questions, don’t you think?
The Demon: I’m Ludus.
Ludus: Why am I here?
Ludus: Hmmm, let’s think about it together!
Ludus: Maybe I’m here because our little army is threatened now by two priests instead of one?
Ludus: I don’t know, maybe?
Ludus: Yes, I think that's the reason for sure.
Ludus: For the fun part…
Ludus: Well…
Ludus: Use that pretty head of yours.

Ludus: Come on. You can do it.  
-> Oh, you mean… No! I won’t crumble under your sinful influence, you demon!
   Ludus: Oh, so you do have some fire in you!
   Ludus: Interesting…
-> With you “fun” doesn’t really seem like a bad idea.
  Ludus: Oh?
  Ludus: Maybe it’ll be easier than I thought.
  Ludus: Good. 

//(ariel_blush)

Ariel was stunned.
All of those years at the seminaries taught him that facing a demon will be fatal.
That if they find you, especially alone, they won't spare you.
There was also that…
How is it possible that the demon appeared inside the church?
This is the home of the Creator.
No sinful creatures should be able to cross the door to this holy place…
So how..?

//(ariel_basic)

Ludus: Hm?
Ludus: Oh, I know, let me guess!

//(ludus silly)

Ludus: You’re probably wondering why I decided to play with you instead of just ending you, right?
Ludus: And this whole church thing must be confusing too…

Ariel: How do you..?

//(ludus basic)

Ludus: Oh, don’t be silly.
Ludus: It’s written all over your pretty face!
Ludus: Those things are actually connected.
Ludus: The mere fact that I can be here.
Ludus: In front of you.
Ludus: In the temple of your beloved Creator, means one thing.
Ludus: The corruption is too strong already. 

//(Ariel blush)

The atmosphere around them turned heavy.
Heavier than before.
Ludus's voice turned deeper.
More serious. 

//(Ariel basic)


Ludus: You see…
Ludus: This is just a building now.
Ludus: Nothing more.
Ludus: Without the followers…
Ludus: Those sacred places lose all their power…
Ludus: That's why I decided to toy with you for a little bit.

Ludus: Because you already lost, priest.   
->  No… No, we didn’t! Love is stronger than you think! In the end, people will always choose the right way! Just you see! 
   Ludus: So you’re delusional as well, I see. 
-> Lost… Maybe you’re right. Those townsfolk are a lost cause anyway…
  Ludus: You’ll make my job so easy. It’s almost cute. 

Ludus: You are so different from any other person I’ve ever encountered.
Ludus: Is it because you're a priest?
Ludus: Maybe. Well, we will have to wait and see, right?
Ludus: I just can’t wait to see you struggle like a little beetle turned on its back. 

Ariel couldn’t even defend himself because the demon was gone.

<<hide ludus>>
<<hide ariel>>

Ariel collapsed on the floor.
Hitting his knees down on the cold stone of the church's flooring. 
He looked up at the altar, the Creator's symbol.
What was he supposed to do?
This was supposed to be an easy task.
Just an ordinary exorcism and conversion.
But today couldn’t possibly prove him wrong more than it did.
What are even his options now?
He can go and talk to Faust.
With his experience and knowledge, they surely will be fine.
On the other hand there's Marchain, a literal angel and a spirit guide that already offered him help.
Maybe that's a more sane thing to do?
But he also met Lilian, who’s so eager to help!
He already started gathering information for him.
Maybe he should ask him for help?
Or maybe…
He should try converting the demon.
Ludus surely is a leader here.
If he’ll be able to convert him, the rest of the demons won't be a problem anymore…
Or..
What if the demon is right?
What if the town is already lost?
So…
What’s the right way? 

...

(tu ekran z wyborem chłopa)

